WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:04.620
Satoshi and Shota face each other in the Kalos League semifinals.

00:03.950 --> 00:13.830
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:05.680 --> 00:08.150
Will Satoshi manage to win against Shota this time?

00:08.940 --> 00:12.310
And which of them will be fighting Alan in the finals...?

00:14.990 --> 00:18.830
Whoa! Gillgard has cut the trees on the field into small pieces!

00:19.440 --> 00:21.100
What are you trying to do, Shota?

00:23.210 --> 00:25.470
Why? Why did it cut down all the trees?

00:25.980 --> 00:28.500
This is Shota we're talking about; he probably has an idea.

00:29.180 --> 00:32.850
You would normally think that he did that to improve his field of vision, but...

00:35.290 --> 00:36.560
Good job, Gillgard.

00:38.400 --> 00:40.310
Let's brace ourselves, Pikachu!

00:45.220 --> 00:50.980
Rival Showdown!
Satoshi Gekkouga VS Mega Jukain!!

00:53.470 --> 00:56.690
Shota-kun is doing some interesting things as well...

00:56.980 --> 01:06.830
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

00:56.980 --> 01:06.830
Z

00:57.390 --> 00:59.860
He's worked out such elaborate tactics.

01:00.580 --> 01:03.780
I wonder what he's planning to try against that Pikachu.

01:07.540 --> 01:08.990
Pikachu, Iron Tail!

01:11.300 --> 01:12.640
King's Shield!

01:19.120 --> 01:19.710
Oh, right.

01:20.190 --> 01:24.050
If I remember right, if we attack now, our attack power will decrease.

01:26.430 --> 01:28.900
In other words, the more we attack, the bigger our disadvantage will become.

01:29.740 --> 01:30.520
This is bad...

01:31.210 --> 01:32.830
That is really troublesome.

01:33.330 --> 01:35.110
He cannot attack carelessly...

01:35.420 --> 01:36.730
Then what should he do?

01:38.580 --> 01:39.790
Sacred Sword!

01:43.050 --> 01:43.360
Evade it!

01:49.770 --> 01:50.290
Pikachu!

01:54.070 --> 01:54.800
Could he be...

01:55.410 --> 01:58.170
...trying to reduce Pikachu's speed?

01:58.750 --> 01:59.500
What do you mean?

02:00.160 --> 02:04.210
The fallen trees make the ground uneven, making it easier for Pikachu to lose its footing.

02:05.230 --> 02:07.140
Gillgard floats, so...

02:07.630 --> 02:09.260
...it has the advantage.

02:09.770 --> 02:11.310
Follow it up with Sacred Sword!

02:14.590 --> 02:15.190
Dodge!

02:24.030 --> 02:24.570
Pikachu!

02:24.990 --> 02:27.360
We cannot have you move around as you please.

02:27.950 --> 02:28.750
Thunderbolt!

02:31.950 --> 02:33.020
King's Shield!

02:42.160 --> 02:42.420
Again!

02:42.910 --> 02:44.830
Pikachu, I have a good idea.

02:45.230 --> 02:47.530
It's risky, but we have to try.

02:48.730 --> 02:50.020
I believe in you.

02:52.170 --> 02:53.790
Satoshi is about to start something.

02:54.340 --> 02:56.190
That is the face he is making.

02:57.200 --> 02:58.830
I have seen it many times before.

03:00.490 --> 03:02.250
Please brace yourself, Gillgard!

03:03.600 --> 03:05.170
Pikachu, Iron Tail!

03:08.750 --> 03:11.290
Pikachu has knocked the trees into the air!

03:11.630 --> 03:13.830
What is the meaning of this?

03:14.510 --> 03:16.450
It is no use. Please use Fury Cutter!

03:17.830 --> 03:18.320
Now!

03:18.600 --> 03:19.360
Use the trees!

03:39.320 --> 03:40.870
I knew you would do that!

03:41.230 --> 03:42.890
Gillgard, King's Shield!

03:44.850 --> 03:45.760
All right, Pikachu!

03:46.040 --> 03:47.220
Throw that piece of wood at it!

03:52.080 --> 03:52.930
Thunderbolt!

03:57.570 --> 03:58.240
Gillgard!

04:02.210 --> 04:03.670
Gillgard is unable to battle!

04:03.950 --> 04:04.990
Pikachu wins!

04:06.720 --> 04:08.590
What a battle!

04:08.590 --> 04:10.860
Preventing King's Shield by lodging a piece of wood there...

04:11.130 --> 04:12.750
I've never seen anything like this!

04:14.070 --> 04:15.730
Pikachu won!

04:17.550 --> 04:19.140
That way of winning is so typical of Satoshi.

04:19.600 --> 04:21.580
Gillgard, thank you for the hard work.

04:22.730 --> 04:23.320
Pikachu!

04:24.680 --> 04:25.440
You did it.

04:26.580 --> 04:28.320
Pikachu has two consecutive victories!

04:28.760 --> 04:34.170
Because three of Shota's Pokémon have been defeated, we will now change the battlefield.

04:34.850 --> 04:36.780
I had no idea this was possible.

04:37.090 --> 04:39.430
And even someone that thought of it would normally never actually do it.

04:39.890 --> 04:40.700
Oh?

04:40.930 --> 04:44.840
Well, if you do not get the timing and exact position right, you cannot...

04:45.480 --> 04:47.510
This guy here can pull it off.

04:48.980 --> 04:49.650
I see.

04:50.270 --> 04:52.530
Satoshi and Pikachu's relationship of mutual trust...

04:53.010 --> 04:55.210
<i>That</i> is Satoshi's strength.

04:56.780 --> 04:59.240
Show me more of yourself!

04:59.920 --> 05:00.410
I will!

05:01.640 --> 05:03.830
All right, the battlefield that has been prepared for them is...

05:04.980 --> 05:06.040
...the badlands!

05:06.740 --> 05:08.730
Both of you, please call out your Pokémon.

05:09.240 --> 05:11.040
Onvern, I choose you!

05:14.490 --> 05:17.770
Satoshi has recalled Pikachu and sent out Onvern!

05:18.350 --> 05:19.490
I'm counting on you, Onvern!

05:20.680 --> 05:21.750
Go, Bohmander!

05:26.420 --> 05:28.910
Shota's fourth is Bohmander.

05:29.190 --> 05:31.670
This is a showdown between two Dragon types!

05:33.310 --> 05:34.960
Bohmander, the Dragon Pokémon.

05:35.720 --> 05:41.100
As a result of its long-held dream of flying, its cellular structure changed, and wings grew on it.

05:41.790 --> 05:43.950
So Komoruu has evolved into Bohmander!

05:44.830 --> 05:46.730
Yeah. It has become stronger.

05:47.780 --> 05:48.610
Begin the battle!

05:49.190 --> 05:50.610
Onvern, Boomburst!

05:53.340 --> 05:53.700
Dodge!

06:02.220 --> 06:03.890
Onvern takes the initiative with Boomburst!

06:04.350 --> 06:05.900
Onvern, Dragon Claw!

06:08.140 --> 06:09.000
Dragon Rush!

06:20.880 --> 06:22.110
Are you all right, Onvern?

06:23.760 --> 06:25.610
We cannot afford any further losses.

06:25.790 --> 06:26.770
Incinerate!

06:30.440 --> 06:30.750
Dodge!

06:37.670 --> 06:38.500
Dragon Tail!

06:43.610 --> 06:46.460
He used the flames from Incinerate to lead Onvern to where he wanted it.

06:47.970 --> 06:48.550
Onvern!

06:49.730 --> 06:50.690
That's the spirit!

06:51.070 --> 06:52.030
Incinerate!

06:52.850 --> 06:53.560
Dodge!

07:00.410 --> 07:01.050
Boomburst!

07:06.120 --> 07:07.560
Now, use Acrobatics!

07:07.980 --> 07:11.600
This is bad. Onvern knows its opponent's location even when they are inside smoke.

07:12.460 --> 07:13.900
Bohmander, please use Protect!

07:18.430 --> 07:19.930
Now, use Dragon Rush!

07:20.160 --> 07:20.910
Acrobatics!

07:39.220 --> 07:39.840
Bohmander...

07:40.370 --> 07:40.920
...and Onvern...

07:41.610 --> 07:42.960
...are both unable to battle!

07:43.340 --> 07:46.180
Both collapsed! It's a draw!

07:48.460 --> 07:50.270
Well done. Take a rest.

07:50.890 --> 07:52.410
Thank you for the hard work, Bohmander.

07:52.990 --> 07:54.440
Peroream, please come out!

07:56.800 --> 07:59.200
Shota's fifth is Peroream!

07:59.720 --> 08:01.300
All right, what about Satoshi?

08:01.440 --> 08:03.580
Numelgon, I choose you!

08:06.080 --> 08:07.120
Incredible!

08:07.610 --> 08:10.350
He's sent out Numelgon, which has a type disadvantage!

08:10.900 --> 08:12.920
Numelgon, it's your first battle in a long time.

08:13.270 --> 08:14.340
Let's go all out!

08:16.430 --> 08:17.480
A Numelgon, huh?

08:18.010 --> 08:20.600
That is the only Pokémon I have never battled.

08:21.860 --> 08:22.940
I have no data on it, so...

08:23.420 --> 08:25.500
Let us brace ourselves, Peroream!

08:28.990 --> 08:29.930
Pokémon Quiz.

08:30.380 --> 08:31.070
The answer is...?

08:32.980 --> 08:42.950
Coming up next:

08:32.980 --> 08:37.950
Satoshi Gekkouga VS Mega Jukain!

08:33.860 --> 08:38.630
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

08:37.980 --> 08:42.950
Who will proceed to the finals with Alan!?

08:51.030 --> 08:52.180
Flamethrower!

08:53.870 --> 08:55.130
Ice Beam!

08:58.350 --> 08:59.260
Dazzling Gleam!

09:03.550 --> 09:07.040
Dazzling Gleam lands a direct hit! It's super effective!

09:09.160 --> 09:10.970
Its durability is impressive.

09:11.530 --> 09:13.250
In that case, how about this?

09:13.600 --> 09:14.670
Fairy Wind!

09:15.770 --> 09:16.360
Bide!

09:21.230 --> 09:22.850
Peroream, please use Cotton Guard!

09:26.070 --> 09:26.900
Fire it!

09:32.670 --> 09:33.120
All right.

09:33.990 --> 09:34.830
Ice Beam!

09:35.820 --> 09:36.940
Flamethrower!

09:41.520 --> 09:42.950
Now it is our turn!

09:43.170 --> 09:44.510
Peroream, Fairy Wind!

09:55.690 --> 09:56.330
Numelgon!

09:57.940 --> 10:00.010
Peroream's sense of smell is amazing.

10:00.520 --> 10:03.270
Even in the smoke, it can find out Numelgon's location.

10:04.570 --> 10:06.680
So it's returning the favor for what Onvern did, huh?

10:09.790 --> 10:10.830
Flamethrower!

10:12.190 --> 10:12.770
Use Bide!

10:17.160 --> 10:17.790
Endure...

10:18.230 --> 10:18.850
Endure it!

10:19.440 --> 10:20.390
<i>They</i> are having a hard time, too.

10:20.810 --> 10:22.850
We are definitely dealing damage.

10:23.230 --> 10:24.710
We will push through with Flamethrower!

10:28.340 --> 10:30.440
Please... Hang in there, Numelgon!

10:30.790 --> 10:31.720
What will happen first...?

10:32.720 --> 10:33.360
Will Peroream push through...

10:33.970 --> 10:34.600
...or will Numelgon endure?

10:40.370 --> 10:44.320
Numelgon has withstood the fierce rush of flames!

10:44.830 --> 10:46.070
Go!

10:48.490 --> 10:49.660
Fairy Wind!

11:00.000 --> 11:01.260
Both are unable to battle!

11:03.000 --> 11:05.400
Another double knockout!

11:05.400 --> 11:10.110
Their respective powers are fighting for dominance! You can't avert your eyes from this battle till the end!

11:11.130 --> 11:12.490
What a battle...

11:12.890 --> 11:15.240
Eureka's heart is gonna burst...

11:15.940 --> 11:17.750
Peroream, thank you for the hard work.

11:18.830 --> 11:20.510
Numelgon, thank you.

11:20.970 --> 11:21.940
Take a long rest.

11:22.760 --> 11:25.080
Who is Shota's last Pokémon?

11:27.470 --> 11:29.380
Jukain, please!

11:36.040 --> 11:37.410
There it is! It's Jukain!

11:37.780 --> 11:39.360
It is Shota's last Pokémon.

11:39.950 --> 11:43.290
But Satoshi only has Gekkouga and a Pikachu that has suffered damage.

11:43.810 --> 11:46.090
On top of that, Jukain mega evolves.

11:46.600 --> 11:48.230
Be careful, Satoshi.

11:48.900 --> 11:50.100
Pikachu, I'm counting on you.

11:52.740 --> 11:55.480
Satoshi has sent out Pikachu!

11:55.840 --> 11:57.430
Pikachu, Quick Attack!

12:00.440 --> 12:01.950
Jukain, do not let it come closer!

12:02.400 --> 12:03.640
Leaf Storm!

12:07.780 --> 12:08.700
Thunderbolt!

12:15.000 --> 12:16.270
Brute force, huh?

12:16.730 --> 12:17.670
Iron Tail!

12:19.990 --> 12:20.910
Leaf Blade!

12:25.670 --> 12:27.090
Frenzy Plant!

12:33.160 --> 12:33.750
Dodge it!

12:38.360 --> 12:39.020
Pikachu!

12:40.660 --> 12:41.850
Pikachu is unable to battle!

12:42.460 --> 12:43.550
Jukain wins!

12:45.280 --> 12:46.040
It lost...

12:46.300 --> 12:47.010
Pikachu lost...

12:47.370 --> 12:51.280
It must have still had a lot of leftover damage from the battle.

12:52.670 --> 12:53.280
Pikachu...

12:53.800 --> 12:55.310
You did your best. Take a long rest.

12:56.850 --> 12:59.800
Now Satoshi only has one Pokémon left as well.

13:00.120 --> 13:02.790
We have finally reached the final round of this battle!

13:03.350 --> 13:04.350
All right, let's go.

13:04.640 --> 13:05.750
You're the last one, Gekkouga.

13:06.080 --> 13:07.150
I choose you!

13:09.720 --> 13:11.430
I have been waiting for you, Gekkouga.

13:11.920 --> 13:13.320
We have finally made it this far.

13:14.030 --> 13:15.300
Sorry to keep you waiting.

13:15.780 --> 13:16.960
This will decide everything.

13:17.640 --> 13:18.970
Let's give it all we've got, Shota!

13:19.230 --> 13:20.530
That is exactly what I want.

13:20.810 --> 13:22.440
Let us not leave any regrets.

13:23.100 --> 13:24.980
Gekkouga, Water Shuriken!

13:28.110 --> 13:29.030
Dragon Claw!

13:36.910 --> 13:37.630
Charge in!

13:37.630 --> 13:38.510
Double Team!

13:40.160 --> 13:41.390
Frenzy Plant!

13:51.630 --> 13:52.170
There it is.

13:52.510 --> 13:53.750
Leaf Blade!

13:55.980 --> 13:56.600
Cut!

14:02.940 --> 14:03.910
This is...

14:04.240 --> 14:05.610
What a breathtaking battle!

14:05.870 --> 14:08.910
This tension is enveloping the entire stadium!

14:09.360 --> 14:10.400
Amazing...

14:12.020 --> 14:12.740
Satoshi...

14:13.450 --> 14:16.020
I have been chasing after him this whole time.

14:16.790 --> 14:20.600
At first, he seemed so far away and so tall.

14:21.470 --> 14:21.800
But today...

14:22.290 --> 14:23.500
If I defeat him here and now,

14:24.050 --> 14:26.290
I believe I will rise even higher.

14:27.070 --> 14:27.520
That is why...

14:28.220 --> 14:30.120
...I wanted to fight the real Satoshi.

14:30.990 --> 14:33.400
And Satoshi came back, just as he promised.

14:34.210 --> 14:35.140
The conclusion of the battle back then...

14:35.740 --> 14:37.060
...will take place now!

14:38.110 --> 14:38.710
Shota...

14:39.240 --> 14:39.790
I'm sorry.

14:40.470 --> 14:41.250
I was in a rush.

14:41.870 --> 14:42.650
I was scared...

14:43.760 --> 14:45.440
You were following me from behind, and I was scared of you.

14:46.520 --> 14:47.060
And then...

14:47.680 --> 14:49.150
...before I knew it, you'd passed me.

14:50.060 --> 14:53.360
But thanks to that, I was able to find myself again!

14:54.120 --> 14:54.830
We'll show you...

14:55.370 --> 14:56.610
...our true selves!

14:57.160 --> 14:58.010
Let's go!

14:58.520 --> 15:00.430
Gekkouga, use your full power!

15:14.250 --> 15:16.710
There it is! It's that strange Gekkouga!

15:18.600 --> 15:20.970
Go, Satoshi Gekkouga!

15:22.500 --> 15:24.100
Jukain, let us go.

15:24.730 --> 15:26.050
Let us give it our all!

15:31.740 --> 15:33.030
Mega evolve!

15:43.600 --> 15:44.770
Jukain has powered up as well!

15:44.990 --> 15:46.480
It has mega evolved!

15:47.110 --> 15:48.320
Frenzy Plant!

15:54.570 --> 15:55.230
Dodge!

15:57.460 --> 15:58.050
Cut!

16:02.470 --> 16:03.640
Water Shuriken!

16:06.560 --> 16:07.690
Dragon Claw!

16:09.830 --> 16:10.870
Aerial Ace!

16:17.550 --> 16:18.890
Leaf Storm!

16:25.070 --> 16:25.960
Leaf Blade!

16:28.340 --> 16:29.140
Cut!

16:39.190 --> 16:40.310
Leaf Storm!

16:47.860 --> 16:48.390
It's not over yet!

16:48.690 --> 16:49.740
Do not let them rest!

16:50.050 --> 16:51.390
Frenzy Plant!

16:57.260 --> 16:58.550
Cut!

17:03.890 --> 17:05.710
Satoshi Gekkouga is under pressure!

17:06.180 --> 17:08.880
They're having trouble closing the distance to Jukain!

17:09.200 --> 17:11.930
How can you get Frenzy Plant to be so powerful?

17:12.190 --> 17:13.500
Really, it is too incredible.

17:14.120 --> 17:15.450
What will happen to Satoshi?

17:15.870 --> 17:16.540
He'll lose...

17:16.980 --> 17:17.580
Don't worry.

17:18.110 --> 17:19.850
Satoshi won't give up till the end.

17:20.340 --> 17:22.510
After all, he's with Gekkouga right now!

17:23.140 --> 17:25.220
Satoshi's strength is to combine the power of two in one.

17:26.000 --> 17:27.690
As long as Satoshi has his Pokémon,

17:28.190 --> 17:30.020
and as long as the Pokémon have Satoshi,

17:30.690 --> 17:33.530
they all become much more powerful!

17:34.230 --> 17:34.880
Cut!

17:38.620 --> 17:41.470
Satoshi-kun is completely one with Gekkouga.

17:41.940 --> 17:42.260
Yes.

17:44.090 --> 17:44.790
Go!

17:46.710 --> 17:47.310
Gekkouga,

17:47.510 --> 17:48.310
Double Team!

17:51.760 --> 17:53.080
Shota, take this:

17:53.590 --> 17:55.710
This is all me and Gekkouga have got!

17:56.010 --> 17:57.340
Water Shuriken!

18:00.490 --> 18:01.050
Jukain,

18:01.390 --> 18:02.630
Leaf Storm!

18:22.710 --> 18:24.200
Jukain is unable to battle!

18:24.650 --> 18:26.810
Therefore, the winner is Satoshi!

18:29.450 --> 18:31.030
It's settled!

18:31.030 --> 18:34.080
Satoshi advances to the finals!

18:36.520 --> 18:37.170
Satoshi!

18:37.380 --> 18:39.550
He won! He won!

18:39.550 --> 18:40.820
I expected nothing less from Satoshi!

18:41.130 --> 18:42.870
Congratulations!

18:42.870 --> 18:44.170
That was awesome, Satoshi!

18:44.350 --> 18:45.050
Congratulations!

18:45.470 --> 18:47.590
You guys were all so cool!

18:49.490 --> 18:50.580
Excellent.

18:50.980 --> 18:52.630
This is what Pokémon battles should be about.

18:52.980 --> 18:58.040
Another big applause to both of them for showing us a passionate battle!

19:01.430 --> 19:02.930
You did it, Gekkouga!

19:06.330 --> 19:08.180
Wow... That brat boy is not bad.

19:08.450 --> 19:09.790
Could he...

19:09.790 --> 19:11.990
...actually win the league?

19:12.360 --> 19:13.470
Marvelous!

19:13.860 --> 19:16.130
That was a truly excellent battle!

19:16.510 --> 19:18.460
I look forward to seeing where these two will go from here!

19:19.120 --> 19:23.000
I would be happy if we came to have many Trainers like them.

19:24.030 --> 19:24.340
Yes,

19:24.900 --> 19:26.180
I agree.

19:35.870 --> 19:37.980
I took it. I took everything you had, Satoshi.

19:38.820 --> 19:41.730
You truly are the Trainer I admired.

19:42.110 --> 19:43.290
It was a good battle.

19:43.910 --> 19:46.470
I was really excited while fighting you too!

19:46.900 --> 19:48.050
Thank you very much.

19:48.730 --> 19:51.380
I will battle more and more, gain a lot of EXP,

19:51.870 --> 19:52.410
and then one day,

19:53.220 --> 19:55.250
I will definitely surpass you, Satoshi.

19:55.610 --> 19:59.060
I'll also battle a lot more and become stronger!

19:59.510 --> 20:00.420
I won't fall behind!

20:00.880 --> 20:02.210
Let's battle again.

20:02.590 --> 20:03.400
Satoshi...

20:04.330 --> 20:05.020
Yes!

20:07.330 --> 20:10.980
The heated battle between Satoshi and Shota is over.

20:11.750 --> 20:14.350
However, they will each continue to gain more EXP,

20:14.670 --> 20:15.890
and they will grow,

20:16.420 --> 20:18.960
and then one day, they will battle again.

20:20.010 --> 20:21.850
All right, the finals are next!

20:22.340 --> 20:23.410
His opponent is Alan!

20:26.300 --> 20:28.490
The very exciting points of the movie!

20:28.490 --> 20:29.580
Get blown away!

20:30.960 --> 21:20.960
The blockbuster is
currently in theaters!

20:31.000 --> 20:34.800
VOLCANION

20:31.190 --> 20:33.650
The star Pokémon of the movie is Volcanion.

20:34.800 --> 20:35.640
Yo, human.

20:36.060 --> 20:37.790
How many times're ya gonna crash into me before yer satisfied?

20:37.950 --> 20:41.970
It hates humans, but ends up linked together with Satoshi with a strange chain.

20:41.970 --> 20:44.300
I don't trust those humans!

20:44.300 --> 20:46.730
It's foulmouthed and a little violent.

20:46.880 --> 20:47.630
However...

20:47.630 --> 20:53.640
All these guys here've been hurt by the lies and selfishness of humans.

20:53.640 --> 20:54.270
You too?

20:54.930 --> 20:56.760
Let's not talk 'bout me.

20:57.130 --> 21:03.320
